	{"id": "shrinking_pond", "acts": [1], "title": "Climate Change",
		"text": "You come upon a small pond, and a water spirit living in it. The pond is shrinking by the day, and the spirit looks up at you with big, worried eyes. \"Could you spare a little water?\" it asks.",
		"options": [
			{"label": "Give it a spell", "pick_spell": true, "by_water": [
				{"chance": 1.0, "text": "The spirit gulps it down and splutters. \"That's not even WET! You dried-up old prune!\" A thirst settles in your throat that no water will fix: Ever Thirsting clings to you.", "do": [{"op": "lose_spell"}, {"op": "artifact_id", "id": "ever_thirsting"}]},
				{"chance": 1.0, "text": "\"Oh! A little drop. Thank you.\" The spirit pushes a few golden leaves out of the mud for you: 50 Leaves.", "do": [{"op": "lose_spell"}, {"op": "amber", "n": 50}]},
				{"chance": 1.0, "text": "\"Ahh, that's lovely! Thank you, thank you!\" The pond rises a finger's width, and the spirit fishes something out of the bottom for you: an artifact.", "do": [{"op": "lose_spell"}, {"op": "artifact_tier", "tier": "common"}]},
				{"chance": 1.0, "text": "The pond swells to its banks with a happy gurgle. The spirit rises up, beaming, and lays a treasure in your hands: a rare artifact.", "do": [{"op": "lose_spell"}, {"op": "artifact_tier", "tier": "rare"}]}]},
			{"label": "Walk away", "outcomes": [
				{"chance": 1.0, "text": "As you turn to leave, the spirit whispers something after you. Your throat goes dry, and it stays dry: Ever Thirsting clings to you.", "do": [{"op": "artifact_id", "id": "ever_thirsting"}]}]}]},
	# The Church of Aole: listen to the last priest's story, then answer his three questions (one wrong answer: the same
	# as walking away, Aole's Small Blessing). All three right: Aole's Blessing, or healed to full if you have it.
	{"id": "church_of_aole", "acts": [1], "title": "The Church of Aole", "text": "By a road that few still walk stands a church half swallowed by ivy. In its doorway waits a priest so ancient he looks as though one strong sneeze would scatter him to dust. \"Greetings, stranger,\" he croaks. \"I am the last follower of Aole. Have you a little time to hear of our goddess and saviour?\"", "options": [{"label": "Stay awhile and listen", "next": {"text": "The priest's eyes light up with delight, as if a century of life had dawned upon him again. His voice rings like a golden bell, full of vigor and pride:\n\nIn ages beyond time, when the world was young and life was younger, a door in heaven opened, and through it slipped a small child. Her name was Aole. By her look, she had seen no more than thirteen winters, and her garb was that of a humble traveler. But judge not a book by its cover, for under that insignificant disguise was the soul of an outer god: a being of vast power and knowledge, who could create, shape and destroy worlds. Worlds like ours, no less.\n\nYet she treated us as nothing but equals. She threw her wings away to walk this path of suffering and struggle alongside us mortals. For countless years, she broke bread with the poorest, held hands with the sickest and cried with the most unfortunate. She was a shield unto the weak and a sword unto the wicked.\n\nHer teaching was one of profound simplicity: be kind to one another, and to yourself. Surely in those mundane words lay boundless wisdom, for they were truly the only secret to the happiness of all.", "options": [{"label": "Go on...", "next": {"text": "Then she lifted her eyes to the whole of creation, beholding it bound in chains of evil and tyranny, from the roots of the mountains to the edges of the sky. She grieved, saying: \"I shall break this prison and set all creation free.\"\n\nWith her rode the Four Horsemen, mighty in power, yet mightier still in devotion. One possessed the hands of a maestro, which could weave life itself into music. One had eyes so sharp that they pierced through all lies and liars alike. One had a beauty so radiant that a mere gaze upon her visage was enough to heal a broken heart. But none could compare to her first horseman, her first disciple, Adam. He needed no sword nor shield, for his devotion to Aole alone saved him from every evil that could befall him on his way.\n\nThat was more than two hundred years ago. None of them returned. The faithful scattered like leaves before the storm, until only I remained to sweep the floor of her house.\n\nYet what is life without faith? I have faith in Aole, and I have faith in you, traveler. Be kind to others and to yourself, and Aole's blessing is upon you. Amen.", "options": [{"label": "Thank you, father", "next": {"text": "The priest falls silent, and peers at you over his spectacles. \"Tell me, stranger: who was Aole?\"", "options": [{"label": "Our lord and saviour", "next": {"text": "\"Yes! Yes, she was.\" The old man's eyes shine. \"And why did she leave us?\"", "options": [{"label": "She abandoned us", "outcomes": [{"chance": 1.0, "text": "The old priest's face falls, but he smiles at you all the same. \"I understand, stranger. Bless your soul.\" A warm breeze follows you out of the church: Aole's Small Blessing. You will start your next fight with 1 extra random Essence.", "do": [{"op": "gift", "els": ["random"]}]}]}, {"label": "To find a way to save this world from evil and tyranny", "next": {"text": "\"Just so, just so.\" He nods slowly. \"And what, then, should a follower of Aole do?\"", "options": [{"label": "Fight evil", "outcomes": [{"chance": 1.0, "text": "The old priest's face falls, but he smiles at you all the same. \"I understand, stranger. Bless your soul.\" A warm breeze follows you out of the church: Aole's Small Blessing. You will start your next fight with 1 extra random Essence.", "do": [{"op": "gift", "els": ["random"]}]}]}, {"label": "Show others kindness", "outcomes": [{"chance": 1.0, "text": "Tears run down the old man's face. \"You have listened with your heart. Take this, then, as she would have wanted.\" He lays his hands on yours, and you learn a spell: Aole's Blessing.", "text_if_owned": "\"I see that you already have Aole's Blessing,\" he says softly. \"Then I shall pray for your safe journey.\" His prayer settles over you like warm light: you are healed to full.", "do": [{"op": "learn_spell", "id": "trade_winds", "else": "heal_full"}]}]}, {"label": "Nothing", "outcomes": [{"chance": 1.0, "text": "The old priest's face falls, but he smiles at you all the same. \"I understand, stranger. Bless your soul.\" A warm breeze follows you out of the church: Aole's Small Blessing. You will start your next fight with 1 extra random Essence.", "do": [{"op": "gift", "els": ["random"]}]}]}]}}, {"label": "I don't know", "outcomes": [{"chance": 1.0, "text": "The old priest's face falls, but he smiles at you all the same. \"I understand, stranger. Bless your soul.\" A warm breeze follows you out of the church: Aole's Small Blessing. You will start your next fight with 1 extra random Essence.", "do": [{"op": "gift", "els": ["random"]}]}]}]}}, {"label": "I don't know", "outcomes": [{"chance": 1.0, "text": "The old priest's face falls, but he smiles at you all the same. \"I understand, stranger. Bless your soul.\" A warm breeze follows you out of the church: Aole's Small Blessing. You will start your next fight with 1 extra random Essence.", "do": [{"op": "gift", "els": ["random"]}]}]}, {"label": "You", "outcomes": [{"chance": 1.0, "text": "The old priest's face falls, but he smiles at you all the same. \"I understand, stranger. Bless your soul.\" A warm breeze follows you out of the church: Aole's Small Blessing. You will start your next fight with 1 extra random Essence.", "do": [{"op": "gift", "els": ["random"]}]}]}]}}]}}]}}, {"label": "Walk away", "outcomes": [{"chance": 1.0, "text": "\"I understand, stranger,\" he says. \"Bless your soul.\" As you leave, a warm breeze follows you down the road: Aole's Small Blessing. You will start your next fight with 1 extra random Essence.", "do": [{"op": "gift", "els": ["random"]}]}]}]},
	# The Flying Turtle: walk away and he falls on your head 3 events later (any act: see RunState.due_events).
	{"id": "flying_turtle", "acts": [1], "title": "The Flying Turtle", "text": "You come across a flying turtle lying upside down on its shell, legs waving in the air, quite unable to get up. He greets you warmly:\n\n\"What are you looking at, potato head? Can't you see I'm in a pickle here? Come and help me out, you slow-witted, big-nosed, bipedal special specimen. Help me, or your father is a hamster and your mother smells of elderberries!\"", "options": [{"label": "Help him", "outcomes": [{"chance": 1.0, "text": "You flip the turtle back onto his feet. He shakes himself off and glares at you.\n\n\"You think you've saved me, but you've only saved yourself from an inevitably painful future. Alright, I have no more use for you, you bipedal fool. Go on, git!\"", "do": []}]}, {"label": "Walk away", "outcomes": [{"chance": 1.0, "text": "\"Yeah, walk away, dummy. One of these days I'll fall on your head. You'll be enjoying the sunny weather when suddenly my heavily armored arse lands on your unflavored face. Maybe it'll look more appealing that way, with the imprint of my majestic behind on your visage. Walk away, dear dimwit. May the light somehow shine upon your bald head.\"", "do": [{"op": "grudge", "event": "turtle_falls", "n": 3}]}]}]},
	{"id": "turtle_falls", "acts": [1, 2, 3], "hidden": true, "title": "Something Is Falling", "text": "You are enjoying the sunny weather when a shadow falls across the path. You look up. Something is falling out of the sky, and it is getting bigger. It is shaped like a turtle.\n\nIt is the flying turtle!", "options": [{"label": "Uh oh...", "outcomes": [{"chance": 1.0, "text": "WHAM! A heavily armored arse lands squarely on your face. The turtle bounces off, rights himself in mid-air and hovers there, cackling. \"Told you so, potato head! Much better. Now that's a face with character!\" He flies off into the sun. You lose 10 HP, and you will be wearing the imprint of his majestic behind for a while.", "do": [{"op": "damage", "n": 10}]}]}]},
	# The Mystery Shed: side with the boy (the Dollar Bill) or the girl (the Half-Eaten Candy), or give them two of your
	# artifacts as new toys for a Mystery Book (each unlocked for good the first time it is found here) (unlocked for good the first time). Three Mystery Books: the spell Summoning Bill.
	{"id": "mystery_shack", "acts": [1], "title": "The Mystery Shed", "text": "You come across a ramshackle Mystery Shed, full of wonders and frauds. Inside, two little twins, a boy and a girl, are fighting over who gets the newest toy from their great-uncle. The moment they see you, they both ask you to be the judge.", "options": [{"label": "Side with the boy", "outcomes": [{"chance": 1.0, "text": "The girl bursts into tears and runs away. The boy, very pleased with himself, rewards you with a crumpled dollar bill. Written across it: \"Wow, this is worthless.\"", "do": [{"op": "artifact_id", "id": "dollar_bill"}]}]}, {"label": "Side with the girl", "outcomes": [{"chance": 1.0, "text": "The boy stomps off, furious with you. The girl thanks you, and hands you the candy she was sucking on. It is half eaten, and a little sticky.", "do": [{"op": "artifact_id", "id": "half_eaten_candy"}]}]}, {"label": "Give each of them a new toy, so they don't have to fight (give 2 artifacts)", "pick_artifact": 2, "outcomes": [{"chance": 1.0, "text": "The kids stop fighting at once to admire their new toys. They thank you together, and press a strange old book into your hands, a six-fingered hand drawn on its cover: the Mystery Book.", "do": [{"op": "mystery_book"}]}]}]},
	# The Wax Witch (every act): each drop of blood costs 20% of your max HP (rounded down, one drop after the other) and
	# puts a purple wax seal on a spell of your choice (you pick the spell, then the Essence to seal).
	{"id": "wax_witch", "acts": [1, 2, 3], "title": "The Wax Witch", "text": "On the horizon stands a purple cloak, draped over a body that isn't there. Its shrivelled finger points at you, and its voice croaks right into your mind without a word being spoken:\n\n\"A drop of blood for a drop of wax.\"", "options": [{"label": "Give one drop of blood", "wax": 1, "outcomes": [{"chance": 1.0, "text": "A single drop of blood rises from your arm and drifts toward the witch. In mid-air it turns to purple wax, and seals itself onto your spell. You feel a little emptier: you lose {n} max HP.", "do": [{"op": "blood", "n": 1}]}]}, {"label": "Give two drops of blood", "wax": 2, "outcomes": [{"chance": 1.0, "text": "Two drops of blood rise from your arm and drift toward the witch. In mid-air they turn to purple wax, and seal themselves onto your spells. You feel a lot emptier: you lose {n} max HP.", "do": [{"op": "blood", "n": 2}]}]}, {"label": "Walk away", "outcomes": [{"chance": 1.0, "text": "You turn your back on the witch. The voice in your head chuckles softly, then falls silent.", "do": []}]}]},
	# The Recycler (every act): give him a spell, an artifact or a bottle; he offers 3 of the same kind and rarity
	# (bottles: of about the same price), and you take one (see RunState.recycle_offer).
	{"id": "recycler", "acts": [1, 2, 3], "title": "The Recycler", "text": "Before you see him, you already hear him. His voice is thunderous and constant, and it never stops: \"REUSE! REDUCE! RECYCLE!\"\n\nThen he comes around the bend, pulling a cart piled high with things other people threw away, and holds out an enormous hand.", "options": [{"label": "Give him a spell", "recycle": "spell", "text": "You take it. \"REUSE!\" he bellows approvingly, and trundles off with his cart. You can still hear him long after he is out of sight."}, {"label": "Give him an artifact", "recycle": "artifact", "text": "You take it. \"REUSE!\" he bellows approvingly, and trundles off with his cart. You can still hear him long after he is out of sight."}, {"label": "Give him a bottle", "recycle": "bottle", "text": "You take it. \"REUSE!\" he bellows approvingly, and trundles off with his cart. You can still hear him long after he is out of sight."}, {"label": "Give him nothing", "outcomes": [{"chance": 1.0, "text": "\"REDUCE!\" he bellows, nodding as if you had done something very wise, and trundles off with his cart.", "do": []}]}]},
	# They See Me Rolling: played on the stage with the bear's own puppet (BearRollScene). Stop him: 50 Leaves and 5 damage.
	# Step aside: the 3rd event after this one is his revenge (any act): a Rolling Bear elite fight, you Stunned the first turn.
	{"id": "rolling_bear", "acts": [1], "title": "They See Me Rolling", "scene": "bear_meet", "text": "Someone is rolling across the road, round and round, back and forth, and they are not stopping.", "options": [{"label": "Try to stop them"}, {"label": "Get out of the way"}]},
	{"id": "bear_revenge", "acts": [1, 2, 3], "hidden": true, "title": "The Bear Comes Back", "scene": "bear_revenge", "text": "You hear something coming. It is fast. Too fast!", "options": [{"label": "Fight!"}]},
	# The Overgrown Vine: cast a spell for the tree (you keep it); what happens depends on its category ("by_kind":
	# Offensive 40 Leaves, Defensive heal 5, Utility nothing).
	{"id": "overgrown_vine", "acts": [1], "title": "The Overgrown Vine", "text": "You find a tree withering in the choking embrace of an overgrown vine. Its leaves are brown, and its branches creak as the vine squeezes tighter.", "options": [{"label": "Cast a spell to help the tree", "pick_spell": true, "keep_spell": true, "by_kind": {"damage": {"chance": 1.0, "text": "You blast the vine away. The tree sheds some leaves for you as its branches tremble with gratitude: 40 Leaves.", "do": [{"op": "amber", "n": 40}]}, "defense": {"chance": 1.0, "text": "You cast a barrier between the tree and the vine. The tree drops a fruit for you as its branches tremble with gratitude. You eat it and heal 5 HP.", "do": [{"op": "heal", "n": 5}]}, "utility": {"chance": 1.0, "text": "Your spell does nothing. The tree is silently disappointed in your uselessness.", "do": []}}}, {"label": "Leave the tree to its fate", "outcomes": [{"chance": 1.0, "text": "You walk on. Behind you, the branches creak a little louder.", "do": []}]}]},
	# The Broken Bridge (Act 2): jump (50%: 1 extra random Essence next fight; 50%: into the bog, and one of your
	# active spells needs 1 more Water for the rest of the run), or go round through the thorns (5 damage).
	{"id": "broken_bridge", "acts": [2], "title": "The Broken Bridge", "text": "You come upon a broken bridge over a small bog. Both banks are thick with thorny bushes, and the gap in the middle looks... jumpable. Probably.", "options": [{"label": "Jump over it", "outcomes": [{"chance": 0.5, "text": "You take a running start and leap. You make it across, heart pounding! You feel so excited that you will start your next fight with 1 extra random Essence.", "do": [{"op": "gift", "els": ["random"]}]}, {"chance": 0.5, "text": "You take a running start and leap... and land with a splash in the middle of the bog. Your spellbook is soaked through: {spell} now needs 1 more Water.", "do": [{"op": "soak"}]}]}, {"label": "Find a way around the thorny bushes", "outcomes": [{"chance": 1.0, "text": "You push your way through the bushes until you find a way around. The thorns don't make it easy: you lose 5 HP.", "do": [{"op": "damage", "n": 5}]}]}]},
	# Elemental Fishing (Act 2): a minute of chanting at Essence fish (FishGame), then the old man's tally.
	{"id": "elemental_fishing", "acts": [2], "title": "Elemental Fishing", "text": "Beside a dark, odorous stream sits a ragged man. It is hard to tell whether the smell comes from the man or from the stream. He is so thin that, had he introduced himself as a walking skeleton, you would not have been surprised.\n\n\"Hi there, stranger,\" he says. \"Would you mind helping me catch some fish? It has been more than two hundred years since I caught any, and as you can see, I am quite hungry.\"", "options": [{"label": "Help him fish", "next": {"text": "\"Wonderful!\" He points a bony finger at the water. \"The fish in this stream are made of Essence, so you catch them with a chant, not a rod. Line up your Essence and Chant: every fish loses the longest start of its row that your chant contains, just like in a fight. You can chant as often as you like, and your three Essence never run out. A whale is worth 10 Leaves, a swordfish 6 and a barracuda 4. You've got one minute!\"", "options": [{"label": "Ready", "minigame": "fish"}]}}, {"label": "Walk away", "outcomes": [{"chance": 1.0, "text": "\"Oh, I see. You are busy,\" he sighs. \"I will just wait another two hundred years, then.\"", "do": []}]}]},
	# The Mausoleum (Act 2): touch one of three lights. Red: +20% max HP (rounded down; healed as much). Blue: 20 Lasting
	# Shield at the start of the next fight. Green: 3 extra random Essence at the start of the next fight.
	{"id": "mausoleum", "acts": [2], "title": "The Mausoleum", "text": "You stumble upon an ancient mausoleum, its doors long since rotted away. Inside, above three stone coffins, three balls of light hang in the dark: one red, one blue, one green. They hum softly, and you feel a strange urge to touch one.", "options": [{"label": "Touch the red ball", "outcomes": [{"chance": 1.0, "text": "The red light floods into your veins, warm as a heartbeat. Somewhere in the coffin below, something sighs. You feel sturdier than ever: +{n} max HP.", "do": [{"op": "max_hp_pct", "pct": 0.2}]}]}, {"label": "Touch the blue ball", "outcomes": [{"chance": 1.0, "text": "The blue light settles over your skin like cold armour, and stays there, waiting. You will start your next fight with 20 Lasting Shield.", "do": [{"op": "lasting_next", "n": 20}]}]}, {"label": "Touch the green ball", "outcomes": [{"chance": 1.0, "text": "The green light leaps into your bag and hides there, giggling. You will start your next fight with 3 extra random Essence.", "do": [{"op": "gift", "els": ["random", "random", "random"]}]}]}]},
	# The Ruined Watchtower (Act 2): what you spot from the top is where you go: a campfire, the merchant, or a fight with
	# a random Act 1 boss (no talk, full boss rewards; the act does not end).
	{"id": "watchtower", "acts": [2], "title": "The Ruined Watchtower", "text": "You find a ruined watchtower. It may be half the height it once was, but in this wasted swamp it is probably still the tallest thing for a hundred miles. You climb to the top and look out over the horizon. There, you see...", "options": [{"label": "A camping site", "outcomes": [{"chance": 1.0, "text": "A thin line of smoke rises from a clearing not far off. You climb down and make your way there: a campfire, still burning, and nobody around to mind it.", "do": [{"op": "room", "kind": "rest"}]}]}, {"label": "A towering monster", "outcomes": [{"chance": 1.0, "text": "Something enormous moves on the horizon. Before you are even halfway down the tower, it has seen you, and it is coming.", "do": [{"op": "room", "kind": "boss"}]}]}, {"label": "The merchant", "outcomes": [{"chance": 1.0, "text": "A familiar cart trundles along the road below. You hurry down the steps and wave it over.", "do": [{"op": "room", "kind": "shop"}]}]}]},
